1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,820
Enemies in Returnal have

2
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:03,320
tentacles that writhe as if alive.

3
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,620
For this kind of effect, the developers used

4
00:00:04,620 --> 00:00:06,880
particles connected to one another.

5
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,720
Connected points follow one another’s motion.

6
00:00:09,720 --> 00:00:13,520
Then we will build a thick surface around them.

7
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,860
Follow the root and tip

8
00:00:14,860 --> 00:00:16,140
of the tentacle separately.

9
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,260
Their motion is not identical at every instant,

10
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,400
which helps the shape feel flexible.

11
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:24,160
The initial approach attached a physical body to each bone.

12
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:27,420
But computation cost and artistic control were difficult.

13
00:00:27,420 --> 00:00:32,060
The team developed the particle structure in a GPU effects tool.

14
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:35,000
The points connect through parent and child relationships.

15
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,040
Adding a physical body along every long chain

16
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:39,120
creates many connections to simulate.

17
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,920
Particles let artists control the motion rules

18
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:43,680
inside their effects tools.

19
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:45,780
Each child references one parent,

20
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:48,840
while a parent can have multiple children.

21
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:52,040
A child uses its parent’s information from one frame earlier.

22
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,100
The parent moves first,

23
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,000
and later points follow with a delay,

24
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,060
producing organic motion.

25
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:58,900
Imagine a line of people, each following

26
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:01,840
the person ahead from a moment earlier.

27
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:03,240
The front has already turned

28
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:05,780
while the back bends a little later.

29
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:08,180
The model’s delayed points

30
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,960
make the parent-child relationship visible.

31
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,220
Moving points alone

32
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:14,440
do not make a thick tentacle visible.

33
00:01:14,440 --> 00:01:18,080
The initial flat ribbons became cylindrical surfaces.

34
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:20,920
Smooth curves are built along the points.

35
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:22,720
Even from the side or in shadow,

36
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:24,560
their volume remains readable.

37
00:01:24,560 --> 00:01:26,220
Turn the ribbon sideways.

38
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,760
Only its thin edge is visible.

39
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,100
A cylinder keeps its round thickness

40
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:31,120
when viewed from different sides.

41
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,080
If the surface twists,

42
00:01:32,080 --> 00:01:34,340
its lighting can rotate strangely too.

43
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:35,940
So the surface orientation

44
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:37,960
is inherited and refined from the parent

45
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,780
using an additional calculation.

46
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:41,180
The motion-driving points

47
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:45,300
and a stable surface built around them are both needed.

48
00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:46,820
Stripes around a tube

49
00:01:46,820 --> 00:01:49,080
make its surface twist easier to see.

50
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:50,620
Smoothly connecting these orientations

51
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,760
also makes changes in lighting smoother.

52
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:53,500
This motion also connects to

53
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:57,500
states such as an enemy preparing an attack.

54
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:58,740
Artists and animators

55
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:01,980
adjusted motion timing so attacks were easy to read.

56
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:05,200
Particles follow the parent’s earlier movement.

57
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:08,560
Together with the surrounding surface, they bring the tentacles to life.

58
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,240
Constantly waving is different from

59
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:13,320
moving in step with an attack preparation.

60
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,200
This motion also helps players

61
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,040
notice an enemy preparing an attack.
